        "Content": "Visit dngflanaganford.ie to register your interest & to see current offers, or place an offer on this property (please note offers can be placed once your registration has been approved, subject to conditions).\r\n\r\nA spacious period townhouse in the heart of Sligo town centre, offering generous room proportions, excellent ceiling heights, and the benefit of a private rear courtyard and outbuilding. The property combines character features with practical accommodation across three levels, making it an ideal town-centre home\r\n\r\nThis is a listed building in the Sligo development plan and features attractive window styling, stone and brickwork to the front, and generous ceiling heights throughout, particularly on the ground floor. The home also benefits from oil-fired central heating to wall-mounted radiators, uPVC double-glazed windows and doors, and a private rear courtyard with a stone and brick-built shed accessed from both the laneway and the rear yard. Some original window shutters remain in place, although they are not functional at present.\r\n\r\nLocation\r\nThe property is set in an ideal position close to Sligo town centre, with OConnell Street approximately 50 m away and all town-centre amenities on the doorstep. An excellent bus stop is located directly across the road, making this a highly convenient location for town living.\r\n\r\nEntrance Hall\r\n6.60m x 1.10m (21.65ft x 3.61ft)\r\nTiled flooring throughout; includes stairwell area\r\n\r\nUtility Room\r\n2.10m x 1.60m (6.89ft x 5.25ft)\r\nOpen plan to hallway; houses washing machine and tumble dryer; access to rear porch\r\n\r\nLiving Room\r\n3.20m x 3.70m (10.50ft x 12.14ft)\r\nLaminate wood flooring, open fireplace with period marble surround, south-facing street-front window, ceiling height 2.7 m\r\n\r\nKitchen/Dining Room\r\n2.50m x 3.60m (8.20ft x 11.81ft)\r\nFully fitted kitchen, overlooks private rear courtyard, tiled splashback, timber wall panelling\r\n\r\nRear Porch\r\n2.40m x 2.00m (7.87ft x 6.56ft)\r\nBlock-built lean-to with access to rear yard\r\n\r\nBedroom 1\r\n3.60m x 2.50m (11.81ft x 8.20ft)\r\nCarpet flooring, south-facing street-front window, generous ceiling height\r\n\r\nLanding\r\n3.70m x 1.00m (12.14ft x 3.28ft)\r\n\r\nMain Bathroom\r\n3.70m x 1.70m (12.14ft x 5.58ft)\r\nFully fitted suite with wash hand basin, toilet, bath and corner shower; fully tiled shower area; newly fitted electric shower\r\n\r\nBedroom 2\r\n2.50m x 3.20m (8.20ft x 10.50ft)\r\nOverlooks the rear courtyard\r\n\r\nLanding\r\n2.90m x 0.80m (9.51ft x 2.62ft)\r\nCarpet flooring to stairs and landing\r\n\r\nBedroom 3\r\n3.60m x 4.20m (11.81ft x 13.78ft)\r\nCarpet flooring, two south-facing front windows, spacious room\r\n\r\nBedroom 4\r\n2.30m x 3.60m (7.55ft x 11.81ft)\r\nCarpet flooring, overlooks private rear courtyard\r\n\r\nShed\r\n2.70m x 3.50m (8.86ft x 11.48ft)\r\nStone and brick-built shed under pitched roof; dual access from laneway and rear courtyard; ideal for storage\r\n\r\nDirections: Eircode F91 KH58"
      },
